From: qcom-vp maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: stop lookahead at the translation limit

An I/O fetch limits a translation block to one instruction.
An aligned fetch records four bytes, even for a compressed instruction.
The page-end lookahead can then record the second halfword again.
Skip that lookahead when the block reaches its instruction limit.
Keep the byte-recording assertions and normal page checks.

--- a/target/riscv/translate.c
+++ b/target/riscv/translate.c
@@ -1575,7 +1575,8 @@
     }
 
     /* Only the first insn within a TB is allowed to cross a page boundary. */
-    if (ctx->base.is_jmp == DISAS_NEXT) {
+    if (ctx->base.is_jmp == DISAS_NEXT &&
+        ctx->base.num_insns < ctx->base.max_insns) {
         if (ctx->itrigger || !translator_is_same_page(&ctx->base, ctx->base.pc_next)) {
             ctx->base.is_jmp = DISAS_TOO_MANY;
         } else {
